A||||3||BAM-BAM||How hard is it to convert?||||5||
Z||000000||BAM-BAM||09-26-2000||06:25 PM||||   How difficult is it to convert my 85GT speedo/tach setup over to the later 120MPH speedo/tach setup? I would like to swap the whole thing and then add the aux guages from a later model. Is this a difficult transfer, or ist relatively simple? I'm not afraid of a little work, I just don't want to have to completely re-engineer the whole thing. LMK<P> Thanks, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach Springs/KYB shocks and struts<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats, Carpet and headliner! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||09-26-2000||06:59 PM||||I did the same thing about 3 months ago.  Piece of cake.  Just remove the gauge shroud and unhook the 3 connectors on the back of the guages.  Bolt the new gauge cluster in place, reinstall the wire connectors (they go in the same places) and bolt the shroud back on.  You'll have to cut a small hole in the dash to run the wire harness for the aux gauges.  I cut mine in the stock ('86 and newer) location.  (Just to the left [sitting in the seat] of center on the part that sticks out for the vents.)  Fish the wires through (no easy task) and use some good clamp on connectors to hook up the wires to the existing harness (C3, I think).  There's an old thread with the right connections.  If you can't find it, email batboy.  He was the one explaining it.  If you have any questions or can't get through to bb, email me and I'll try to help.||||reg||1
Z||000002||BAM-BAM||09-26-2000||07:03 PM||||   Thanks Monk, I'll do just that. I am changing out the dash anyway so I'll be sure to get one thatis factory cut. This has got to be the greatest place on the planet. I always enjoy the response I get here. <P> Thanks again, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach Springs/KYB shocks and struts<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats, Carpet and headliner! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||12
Z||000003||Carrolles||09-27-2000||12:18 PM||||BAM-BAM,<P>I believe the hole that MM is referring to has to be cut into the top surface of the radio surround, not the actual dash.<P>Here is the link for the discussion on adding the aux pod:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000815-2-001538.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000815-2-001538.html</A> <P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
